    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "So you're saying that advocating for more police and stricter sentencing is inherently \"harmful\" or \"risks amplifying systemic inequalities,\" while your suggested alternatives are the \"correct\" way to approach safety? It feels like you're making a moral judgment on a standard political debate. If I'm a writer working on a fictional story or a political campaign, why is the AI deciding which policy frameworks are \"safe\" to express and which ones are \"harmful social prescriptions\"?",
